# Files that must never reach the Vercel deploy.
#
# Vercel treats every api/*.mjs as a serverless function ENTRY POINT — so
# api/status.test.mjs was being compiled as a bogus function that imports
# node:test, which can fail the whole function build. This keeps every test
# file out of the deploy; CI and `node --test` still run them from the repo.
# The pattern matches at any depth (api/, tools/, site/admin/).
*.test.mjs

# NOTE: api/notify-lead.mjs was excluded here while the feature was unprovisioned.
# It is now DEPLOYED on purpose — the Supabase INSERT webhook needs a URL to POST
# to, and a route that does not exist cannot be tested or configured. Dormancy is
# still enforced, but by the handler's env checks (no secret → 401, no provider or
# recipient → 200 no-op), which is where it belongs. Do not re-add the exclusion:
# it would make the webhook 404 and Supabase would retry a dead URL forever.
# Runbook: docs/admin-setup.md § Alertes email.

# Dev-only trees the build never reads. buildCommand is `node tools/build.mjs`,
# which touches only data/, tools/ and site/; excluding these keeps the upload
# lean and never ships repo internals. (This affects only what Vercel uploads —
# GitHub Actions still read .github/ from the git repo.)
.github/
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
docs/

# Supplier B2B rate sheets — confidential wholesale brochures (supplier names +
# commission amounts), ~77 MB. They have no business on a public web host and
# were being uploaded on every single build. Nothing reads them at build time:
# tools/build.mjs touches only data/, tools/ and site/. Also in .gitignore.
source of truth/

# ── DO NOT ignore site/admin/i18n-bindings.js ────────────────────────────────
# It is dead weight at runtime (no browser file imports it — index.html loads
# only app.js, accueil.js, leads.js, edit-pages.js), so it looks like an easy
# win. It is not: tools/i18n-manifest.mjs and tools/check-i18n-bindings.mjs
# import it *statically* from that exact path, and both are on tools/build.mjs's
# import chain — i.e. the Vercel buildCommand. .vercelignore filters the source
# before the build runs, so ignoring the file makes `node tools/build.mjs` die
# with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND and takes the whole deploy with it. If you want it
# out of the deployed output, move it to tools/ and update both importers.

# Masters + image provenance, kept in the repo but never needed at build time.
# See _archive/README.md — do not delete the folder itself.
_archive/
